    <td  bgcolor="#c0c0c0" width="100%" valign="top"><tt><font color="#000000">
Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Clunch">Clunch</a>&nbsp;(---.TYLR.splitrock.net)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;06-10-01 04:26<br>
<br><HTML>Last week we had officer meeting and here are the things we discussed-<br>
<br>
First of all, I would like to welcome our new officers-Kalamian,Bindail, and Espirius<br>
<br>
Second, we approved the alliance with Concillium (formerly Wizards of Norrath)<br>
this move is going to help us in ways that even I don't realize yet, just trust me on this one.=)<br>
<br>
And lastly(is that a word?), A NEW RULE!!!!!!!<br>
Cursing in guild chat will no longer be allowed!!!!! This was a rule intended to keep our less mature members from cussing at other members, however, extreme cursing (no matter who it is to) will be grounds for dismissal. As we will be alligning with Concillium, this rule will extend to their guild as well. What this means is-say you get mad at this weekends alliance meeting at start cussing at one of the Concillium,plz just go ahead and remove yourself from guild and save me the trouble. As some of you may or may not realize I have a BIG problem with telling others what to do,BUT recently i have seen language that has no place in a guild of Honor. This rule was installed to increase the enjoyment of ALL, not to try and regulate what we as a group are saying. <br>
<br>
<br>
On a final note, the last hour of the meeting was spent just recalling the old times of the guild and i do beleive we all thuroughly enjoyed it. On that note we will be having a guild meeting soon for the sole purpose of getting together to shoot the breeze, get drunk, whatever. Just some time to get together nd hang out.<br>
<br>
<br>
Long Live the Militia!!!!!<br>
<br>
      C</HTML></font></tt><p>
